 34S  c  J|p=3/2+ for {+35}Cl ground state (2026Su18).                          
 34S  c  1969Pu03: {+35}Cl(d,{+3}He) with a 23.35-MeV deuteron beam from the    
 34S 2c  Argonne cyclotron. The target was enriched {+35}Cl lead chloride target
 34S 3c  on thin C backing. Reaction products were detected using a |DE-E       
 34S 4c  counter covering the angular domain from 12|' to 30|'. Measured        
 34S 5c  |s(E({+3}He),|q). Deduced 11 levels, J, |p, L-transfers, spectroscopic 
 34S 6c  factors from the zero-range JULIE-DWBA analysis of the angular         
 34S 7c  distributions.                                                         
 34S  c  1968Wi20: {+35}Cl(d,{+3}He) with a 34.5-MeV deuteron beam from the Oak 
 34S 2c  Ridge isochronous cyclotron. The target was NaCl evaporated onto carbon
 34S 3c  backing. The reaction products were detected using a solid-state |DE-E 
 34S 4c  telescope. Measured |s(E({+3}He),|q). Deduced 9 levels, J, |p,         
 34S 5c  L-transfers, spectroscopic factors from the zero-range DWBA analysis of
 34S 6c  the angular distributions.                                             
 34S  c  1962Cu07: {+35}Cl(d,{+3}He) with a 15 MeV deuteron beam. Targets were  
 34S 2c  C{-4}H{-5}Cl{-2} with evaporated Au. The reaction products were        
 34S 3c  analyzed by a magnetic spectrometer and detected in its focal plane by 
 34S 4c  a CsI crystal. Measured |s(E({+3}He),|q). Deduced two levels, J, |p,   
 34S 5c  L-transfers, spectroscopic factors from the zero-range SALLY-DWBA      
 34S 6c  analysis of the angular distributions.                                 
 34S  c  1974Cl09: theoretical discussion on the {+35}Cl(d,{+3}He){+34}S        
 34S 2c  reaction.                                                              
